.TH GODOT\-CLI 1 "2026-09-03" "godot-cli 0.9.0" "godot-cli Manual"
.SH NAME
godot\-cli \- Create, edit, and manipulate Godot scenes and resource files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B godot\-cli
[\fIglobal options\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIcommand options\fR] [\fIargs\fR...]
.br
.B godot\-cli
\fB\-\-request\fR \fIjson\fR
.br
.B godot\-cli
\fB\-\-request\-file\fR \fIpath\fR
.br
.B godot\-cli
\fB\-\-request\-stdin\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads and writes Godot 4 scene
.RB ( .tscn ),
resource
.RB ( .tres ),
and
.B project.godot
files with the same identifiers, ordering, and Variant formatting the Godot
editor writes, so files it produces are byte-comparable with editor saves.
.PP
Commands form a tree. Anything expressible on the command line is also
expressible as a JSON request document, and with
.B \-\-json
every command returns one JSON envelope on standard output.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Show version and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose logging on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-request\fR \fIvalue\fR
Run using a JSON command descriptor
.TP
\fB\-\-request\-file\fR \fIpath\fR
Read JSON command descriptor from a file
.TP
\fB\-\-request\-stdin\fR
Read JSON command descriptor from stdin
.SH COMMANDS
.SS godot\-cli help
Show help for a command
.SS godot\-cli ping
Framework health check
.PP
Returns a trivial response so callers can verify JSON and CLI
wiring.
.SS godot\-cli uid
Godot\-compatible resource and scene ID helpers
.SS godot\-cli uid encode
Encode a numeric Resource UID to uid:// text
.PP
Converts a 63\-bit integer to Godot's uid:// representation.
.TP
\fIid\fR
Numeric UID to encode
.SS godot\-cli uid decode
Decode uid:// text to a numeric Resource UID
.TP
\fIuid\fR
uid:// text to decode
.SS godot\-cli uid create\-for\-path
Deterministic Resource UID for a project path and file
.PP
Matches ResourceUID.create_id_for_path using project name,
Godot resource path, and file bytes.
.TP
\fIfile\fR
Scene or resource file (.tscn or .tres)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-name\fR \fIvalue\fR
Project application/config/name
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-path\fR \fIvalue\fR
